From: Andrei Vladescu <52881237+AndreiVladescu@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] policy: prefer 5 GHz when choosing a roam target

When several APs qualify as a better candidate, the one with the strongest
signal was picked. 2.4 GHz always measures louder, so clients were roamed to
the 2.4 GHz radio of the target node and band steering had to move them to
5 GHz again ~20 s later. Give 5 GHz candidates a 10 dB bonus when ranking
qualifying candidates (whether to roam at all is unchanged).

--- a/policy.c
+++ b/policy.c
@@ -113,6 +113,13 @@ is_better_candidate(struct sta_info *si_
 	return reasons;
 }
 
+/* rank qualifying candidates: 5 GHz gets a 10 dB bonus over 2.4 GHz */
+static int
+candidate_rank(struct sta_info *si)
+{
+	return si->signal + (si->node->freq > 4000 ? 10 : 0);
+}
+
 static struct sta_info *
 find_better_candidate(struct sta_info *si_ref, struct uevent *ev, uint32_t required_criteria, uint64_t max_age)
 {
@@ -146,7 +153,7 @@ find_better_candidate(struct sta_info *s
 			ev->select_reasons = reasons;
 		}
 
-		if (!candidate || si->signal > candidate->signal)
+		if (!candidate || candidate_rank(si) > candidate_rank(candidate))
 			candidate = si;
 	}
 
